From f5bb19fe6a935c7968c85693203be61adc456bd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: johnmart19 <johnivan19999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:21:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs-tools: Use shared C++ runtime for sload

Match the runtime used by shared Android dependencies. The static/shared
runtime mix aborted with std::bad_cast even for help/version invocation.
The shared-runtime binary starts correctly with SELinux enforcing.

Co-authored-by: codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 Android.bp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index b18e7c7..44d6512 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -268,7 +268,7 @@ cc_binary {
             ],
         },
     },
-    stl: "libc++_static",
+    stl: "libc++",
 }
 
 cc_binary {
-- 
2.53.0

